+FineSplat was introduced in 2026 by [S1, unofficial]. It is designed for novel view synthesis on datasets like DL3DV, RealEstate10K, and Mip-NeRF 360. The method addresses the trade-off between fine-grained detail preservation and computational cost in feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting. It builds on the principles of differentiable rendering and feed-forward prediction established in earlier works like [15832-feed-forward-and-generalizable-prediction.md].
 
